ion process. The small Balkan state is being seen as a frontrunner among six regional candidates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North and South Korea trade accusations over landmines that injured three soldiers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83bfab4786f1db0adfab8af17ae950b584a77089b8184dfad606a76bfd9fa7bf</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-and-south-korea-trade-accusations-over-landmines-that-injured-three-soldiers/a-79503854--57b9ec347358.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-and-south-korea-trade-accusations-over-landmines-that-injured-three-soldiers/a-79503854?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A mine blast that injured three South Korean soldiers has renewed scrutiny of North Korea's actions along the border and raised questions about its strategic goals.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Zimbabwe tycoon Wicknell Chivayo dies in helicopter crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:130f2333d4bfc3b4e6f1cac3aee4db4ab91d38a7c8529069973909cd872661d3</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zimbabwe-tycoon-wicknell-chivayo-dies-in-helicopter-crash/a-79501691--7a89acb12ffe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zimbabwe-tycoon-wicknell-chivayo-dies-in-helicopter-crash/a-79501691?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Zimbabwe's President Emmerson Mnangagwa has confirmed the death of businessman Wicknell Chivayo and his wife in a helicopter crash, calling the high-rollers with a lavish lifestyle "consummately philanthropic."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump unveils South Korean investment in US energy projects</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:583275742511e21360ad9af6a40d9e802c53dda56847e4686e7443b95d2d7f8c</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-unveils-south-korean-investment-in-us-energy-projects/a-79502998--c02d83badb6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-unveils-south-korean-investment-in-us-energy-projects/a-79502998?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump said South Korea has agreed to invest in an LNG project in Alaska, but Seoul has said it will only proceed once certain conditions are met.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>A brutal assault reignites fears over women's safety in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e4143573ff59466e06863016697118c0eda6b180eacba0ac1141bc2e31ae588</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471--bceecddefb45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A string of sexual assault cases has revived questions about women's safety in India, fuelling fear, protests and demands for action.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could see drivers pay higher running costs while also increasing carbon emissions.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da1ef4fbc040be22dacde732827d77ccf78517900af57bb03b617dff4d80665a</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T11:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-/a-79496554--0804b7619722.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-costs-while-also-increasing-carbon-emissions/a-79496554?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could yet see drivers pay higher running costs while increasing planet-heating emissions.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>UAE launches Flydubai hijacking and terrorism investigation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b503c4aeb0a401ac574cb11c2647c27090c208f4a7b740ffce2b28ccb702e86a</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T10:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uae-launches-flydubai-hijacking-and-terrorism-investigation/a-79497746--17ff1e197de5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uae-launches-flydubai-hijacking-and-terrorism-investigation/a-79497746?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UAE's chief prosecutor said it's looking at the possibility of "terrorist activity or intent" in the alleged attempted hijacking of a Flydubai commercial flight to Tel Aviv. It says it has jurisdiction in the case.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germans' biggest fear is the high cost of living, an annual study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb69a0260329f4a7a0e488d5fb02a17e0600f8496ca752e6a76f79a06b9c88de</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germans-biggest-fear-is-the-high-cost-of-living-an-annual-study-finds/a-79497762--40495e454721.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germans-biggest-fear-is-the-high-cost-of-living-an-annual-study-finds/a-79497762?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">What do Germans fear most in 2026? Wars? Global crises? Wrong. Their biggest concern is the cost of living, which keeps rising.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan launches deadly airstrikes on Afghanistan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c1d043d1b915b01d63e2096bd3ccd56d94a9a930ad00727510a3663e64f865d</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-launches-deadly-airstrikes-on-afghanistan/a-79498092--42bd1620b7f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-launches-deadly-airstrikes-on-afghanistan/a-79498092?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Taliban government in Afghanistan said at least nine civilians were killed in Pakistani airstrikes on two provinces overnight. Pakistan said it had struck militant hideouts, killing 22 fighters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Cristiano Ronaldo walks out of Portugal camp</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9ddb22e26e3a5ac45b029f8b10329304c5148e00ef4d8f94e18a88a80454d22</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cristiano-ronaldo-walks-out-of-portugal-camp/a-79497238--be4e02847569.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cristiano-ronaldo-walks-out-of-portugal-camp/a-79497238?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cristiano Ronaldo has left Portugal’s camp after learning that he would not start the next Nations League match. Portugal's coach has denied reports of a rift between himself and the star player.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Tennessee halts woman's execution after 'failed' attempt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:449757431cccbab924341e23880eda95147a950127f5d71c5a358d83a3a0c75d</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T07:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tennessee-halts-woman-s-execution-after-failed-attempt/a-79496561--90352fa2ac40.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tennessee-halts-woman-s-execution-after-failed-attempt/a-79496561?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike was found alive and snoring, despite being administered two injections of a lethal drug. The state governor has ordered a review of the botched execution.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Berlin leftists seek to pave way for coalition</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c6fe3b6e0aed5e82f60c7fac7d284d78e563857f91325e86a2aaa527ff8e583</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T06:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-leftists-seek-to-pave-way-for-coalition/live-79496180--ffa005d1dac5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-leftists-seek-to-pave-way-for-coalition/live-79496180?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Berlin Left Party, Greens and SPD are to meet to clarify controversial issues ahead of possible coalition talks. The second fuel tax cut this year has come into force as gas and diesel prices spiral. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Swiss glaciers lose more than 5% in ice volume in 2026</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2f7390380f7211afb158fe0fbb075a36fae1eee58129b23b5ca581638a62023</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T03:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/swiss-glaciers-lose-more-than-5-in-ice-volume-in-2026/a-79495965--ebd2291f40e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/swiss-glaciers-lose-more-than-5-in-ice-volume-in-2026/a-79495965?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the last five years, Swiss glaciers have lost nearly 20% of their mass, and 2026 saw the second-biggest loss of glacier volume on record. Experts warn there could be no ice left in the next 10-15 years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US military cuts generals, admirals by 20%, Hegseth says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64404e2fa310223964ac21202b636787726dc634945dfe912e1f18b6aca8bab3</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T01:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-military-cuts-generals-admirals-by-20-hegseth-says/a-79495683--79e31e8a192e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-military-cuts-generals-admirals-by-20-hegseth-says/a-79495683?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US defense secretary has also unveiled major changes, including a new drone command and an Elon Musk-led task force to assess the future of warfare.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Hundreds arrested as student protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbe4ae92f1fdd29bb4b3efa712ff5a14873ec31ddcb137d922fed94051437b6c</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633--b363f8aabae5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Student protests have grown in scale and intensity, with violent clashes in some places leading to hundreds of arrests and dozens of injuries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gaza: NGO reports dire camp conditions, says Israel is moving 'Yellow Line'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85baa92b6e5e0cfefdcc66302d71243eeba9c1bb5d569c49bbe4c664cf3047ef</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T22:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gaza-ngo-reports-dire-camp-conditions-says-israel-is-moving-yellow-line/a-79488777--aae790bffc81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gaza-ngo-reports-dire-camp-conditions-says-israel-is-moving-yellow-line/a-79488777?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Danish Refugee Council alleges that Israel is employing "a policy of protracted displacement" in Gaza. It says the so-called "Yellow Line" is creeping west toward the coast, preventing many from returning home.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Five EU states plan first deportation center in Africa for 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8800320a51cd0dac8fdb0b11df66cc15e04bb8b479eae88870b0cf776a4598f6</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162--dbd1d60c3bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greece, Germany, Austria, Denmark and the Netherlands are moving forward with plans to establish deportation centers for rejected asylum seekers outside the EU.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Flydubai pilot investigated over possible attempt to crash Tel Aviv-bound flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d131ff4acfbed1ab410b0071e56a81f72efcdc57c1f9ccec48cd70805982a262</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flydubai-pilot-investigated-over-possible-attempt-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-flight/a-79484761--24ed602fb272.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flydubai-pilot-investigated-over-possible-attempt-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-flight/a-79484761?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Flydubai service from the UAE to Israel made an emergency landing after the copilot stabbed the captain. Eyewitnesses said he attempted to crash the plane before he was subdued by passengers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France, Spain welcome idea of UK rejoining EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bebd9698633ab7d533db4016a06a62202d8d430152fd55b1088bee5388ee73db</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:33:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T17:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-macron-spain-s-sanchez-welcome-idea-of-uk-rejoining-eu-after-burnham-remarks/a-79493469--0632af9b0576.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-spain-welcome-idea-of-uk-rejoining-eu/a-79493469?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During a visit to Spain, France's Emmanuel Macron said it would be "good news" if the UK moves towards the EU, with Pedro Sanchez also embracing the idea. UK PM Andy Burnham has not ruled out rejoining the bloc.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany debates alleged antisemitism in the Left Party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad193b12f75d5a45fb8f37d6a14b8ba503850258abb4c16a3756fb56b884398d</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-debates-alleged-antisemitism-in-the-left-party/a-79493282--492f53fcd817.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-debates-alleged-antisemitism-in-the-left-party/a-79493282?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Central Council of Jews in Germany thinks the Left Party is dangerous. Other Jews, however, are showing solidarity with the party. How does that add up?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal's Youth Olympics makes Olympics in Africa 'logical'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcd2831cc3b93541d2cc23a94aee9b216e3ee0ba2977ab19218babfdcbb9c836</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975--7dbe2801c775.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Youth Olympics are to be hosted in Africa for the first time ever. The edition in Senegal is also a chance to prove the continent can host a full Olympics in the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City Premier League charges: What do they mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc2f4e75352184c06cbe59c81753e6cdbfde354cbfc59359cefe94088e5c1df9</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638--5f423a99075f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since being bought by the UAE in 2008, Manchester City have become one of the world's most successful football clubs. A raft of serious financial charges threatens to undermine this and bring chaos to the Premier League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ce2dd8df997c586195739f1501381a481a3d51c99743092bf6f9dec5119ac67</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia elections: Polls overshadowed by exhaustion, exodus and geopolitics as ethnic politics eclipse real problems</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f6d85381af3ead9c436796ea87ff06fcaf6e951cc9ae430b9beb026c345e168</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-/a-79487802--91e658c381f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-real-problems/a-79487802?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia goes to the polls on October 4 to elect several parliaments and presidents. While voters worry about the economy and emigration, the campaign is focused on ethnicity, exposing the country's political paralysis.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is US President Donald Trump right to rename AI as 'Super Intelligence'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:215149488582d30ce9a491d8c48b614c46c5dd61ee2d901b1c71ff5c86b7cb4e</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388--e5323453fe90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump thinks the name artificial intelligence sounds "fake" and has ordered US agencies to use "Super Intelligence" instead. Yet, tech firms and researchers have little reason to play along.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland will boycott Eurovision again because of Israel's participation, but the song contest is still expanding.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97904dfaa4bf8b1e1a38d5b60a8d487215936176644386adeae7cfa0c28b494b</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-stil/a-79401752--f96894bb90e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-still-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Volkswagen ends collective wage agreements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eab2725eca841d9dab87a765b4276a814196757f8980ba858ac1b29c01d0e60d</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-ends-collective-wage-agreements/live-79481802--2228595954e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-ends-collective-wage-agreements/live-79481802?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In an effort to cut costs, automaker Volkswagen terminated most of its collective wage agreements in Germany. This could reignite disputes with employee representatives.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino is a 'postcard from the future' — and could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4560c5665c22c6ceee76c1033a06c689b295038438190401876976b21d2a3adb</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945--e1a2336874a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The current El Nino could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths. Researchers warn it offers a glimpse of temperatures that may become normal within 20 years.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary's reckoning with Orban's corrupt system picks up speed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9494ae088f8fb7e554febd4108890f2d934dbf15aa543998731f8116e767d6f</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T04:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed/a-79473714--fef6c98dbd47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed/a-79473714?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's Prime Minister Peter Magyar vowed to dismantle Orban's corrupt networks. High-profile figures are being arrested and many Hungarians are pushing for swift accountability, but the rule of law takes time.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Park satirist pushes for accountability in Cornell gang-rape lawsuit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27ab0938deb5ab5057c53a82e19d21ae5acc3d4829d9da4149eb1a095719da93</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382--e2bb4e991ce2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Writer Toby Morton is using a new website to amplify allegations in a high-profile sexual assault lawsuit involving seven Cornell students. The reopening of the case is causing an outcry on social media.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham seeks 'hope again' at Labour Party conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa1e8762c2098168fbd9beff19a25d8c1399aa2ea5ab667557b75a501256794d</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376--71e603fc9e60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Andy Burnham is seeking a delicate balance between optimism and realism at Labour's annual party conference. He promised hope and an end to "politics as usual" but also an "honest conversation" about difficult dilemmas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: As corruption cases multiply, experts question whether the anti-corruption drive is addressing the causes or just the symptoms.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bced569a13d01cc95491550a4eeffff354243ef8b9dd516c33e94fdcbda3792e</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-as-corruption-cases-multiply-experts-question-whether-the-anti-corruption-drive-is-addressin/a-79473031--8c7e71b0b3b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-as-corruption-cases-multiply-experts-question-whether-the-anti-corruption-drive-is-addressing-the-causes-or-just-the-symptoms/a-79473031?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From a former president to the ex-intelligence chief, Albania is prosecuting senior officials at a rate once thought impossible. But do more prosecutions mean less corruption or simply better enforcement?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Global trade weathers Iran, Ukraine and Trump's tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6787f87035fd567baf07d101deb587be8edadd8772eeb003295dc6b51dd91ec2</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643--538fe77d9a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past six years, COVID, two wars and Donald Trump's tariffs have shaken world trade. With globalization already stalling, is this a temporary shock or the start of a great reversal?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>AI: Concern as Germany plans to double data center capacity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a85d1dda1d6debaae0e27e8c57a3b5450395494aa6dc48ad9cd312927dcc9e2</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-concern-as-germany-plans-to-double-data-center-capacity/a-79407981--ddf2b388dfde.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-concern-as-germany-plans-to-double-data-center-capacity/a-79407981?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany is rewriting the rules to attract data center investment from AI companies. But local communities are becoming increasingly skeptical.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Spain grows fruit and vegetables for Europe, but it's running out of water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da120504125940a2f808805887734780628842d7b5687dfea7f8219e45372a18</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T09:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-grows-fruit-and-vegetables-for-europe-but-it-s-running-out-of-water/a-79399905--7611f918b844.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-grows-fruit-and-vegetables-for-europe-but-it-s-running-out-of-water/a-79399905?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's southern coast produces up to 25% of Europe's fruit and vegetables. But amid intensive farming, climate change and illegal wells, the water it takes to grow them is drying up.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>UK: US government questions bail for Fairford base suspects</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4f7e725917f3c8c3d7c55b69d728b2c9d4edd463d8d06c133d7819219512e1b</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T08:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-us-government-questions-bail-for-fairford-base-suspects/a-79468803--3794b4b54f63.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-us-government-questions-bail-for-fairford-base-suspects/a-79468803?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US government sees "the hand of a foreign actor" in the security scare at RAF Fairford, a hub for US heavy bombers in Europe. Donald Trump criticized the suspects being released on bail amid ongoing investigations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sicily: Mount Etna ash disrupts Catania flights again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8cf5b2b900a117ebf9bb4b1080b75f8a16de75d55dbf27e59932f4c00fc1fbf</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sicily-mount-etna-ash-disrupts-catania-flights-again/a-79462773--6d2664a469ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sicily-mount-etna-ash-disrupts-catania-flights-again/a-79462773?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A thick ash cloud from Mount Etna has been disrupting flights to Catania in Sicily for several days. Italy and Europe's most active volcano, Etna has impacted air travel several times this summer.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Comedian convicted for 'insulting' Erdogan in show</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee7eafc2c3f55cf0bb8ac664583bdd06a0b7f06c793c785f7faa648e8268bbc3</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-comedian-convicted-for-insulting-erdogan-in-show/a-79455759--b32d8c83cb81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-comedian-convicted-for-insulting-erdogan-in-show/a-79455759?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Deniz Goktas was convicted of two of three charges, including "insulting" the president, but was released pending the appeal process. Nominally, Turkey is a secular country with free speech.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What do Manchester City's charges mean for German football?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32294c273c21fdb7c40af21500d79b66bca8d1e4e758bf8a67ffe4537007089e</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-do-manchester-city-s-charges-mean-for-german-football/a-79460412--ba8ebfa60874.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-do-manchester-city-s-charges-mean-for-german-football/a-79460412?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manchester City have reportedly been found guilty of major financial rule breaches. What does this mean for German football?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: COVID vaccine maker BioNTech to close 3 sites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f86ec5a5dd635b5b5f8e128b20f7b4101fe60b1063d1066c295b34c8f391ba77</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-covid-vaccine-maker-biontech-to-close-3-sites/live-79453904--006a9a717608.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-covid-vaccine-maker-biontech-to-close-3-sites/live-79453904?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">COVID-19 vaccine maker BioNTech is to close three sites in Germany after efforts to find buyers failed. Meanwhile, Rhine water levels have fallen to record lows after an unusually dry September. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Diesel prices are surging putting further pressure on Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4e074813b39962da095dec7af1e9ef472fdde8fdb23ef2c5611cfae4f29a867</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/diesel-prices-are-surging-putting-further-pressure-on-europe/a-79390992--edb37306aa00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/diesel-prices-are-surging-putting-further-pressure-on-europe/a-79390992?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trucks, farms and industry are powered with diesel. Now prices are soaring due to refinery disruptions, supply shortages and geopolitical tensions. A potential US export ban could make Europe's diesel crunch even worse.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Will Jürgen Klopp's charisma be enough for Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0acf3a3cacca84e01423929cf7c5c2909532fa22da7eed32841a6698ca9fae</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T09:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-j_rgen-klopp-s-charisma-be-enough-for-germany/a-79455266--fed309f9f1f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-jürgen-klopp-s-charisma-be-enough-for-germany/a-79455266?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After defeat to Greece, Jürgen Klopp faces the first real test of his tenure as coach of Germany's national men's football team. Can his charisma alone push this group forward?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland beat Israel 3-0 in Nations League match overshadowed by political controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1267253d3137e9b227f61790d66bbdb0289683cb969ce5ab274b45a43ea75c47</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-beat-israel-3-0-in-nations-league-match-overshadowed-by-political-controversy/a-79455254--ac737f0c12b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-beat-israel-3-0-in-nations-league-match-overshadowed-by-political-controversy/a-79455254?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ireland easily beat Israel in a Nations League fixture that 24 hours earlier appeared in doubt. One Irish player pulled out of the match to express his opposition to Israel's actions in the Gaza Strip.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>What would Francis of Assisi make of his fame today?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73b8422c9fd2aa9dc7307a38e852c90cdad8e4db86dbbd5fa4ae56b0cfead0e2</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T06:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-francis-of-assisi-make-of-his-fame-today/a-79346151--db42471ab90e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-francis-of-assisi-make-of-his-fame-today/a-79346151?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Catholic saint renounced wealth and fame to become a mendicant friar. Yet throughout history, his teachings and life have inspired popes, Dante and even Mussolini.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>European cities seek ways of boosting affordable housing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:307fb6b78f8d4c8fe1be9bea4e6454d3fca9fc25bb1dde6be6fbf9682fa32ff5</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-cities-seek-ways-of-boosting-affordable-housing/a-79438939--fc67dbf8271c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-cities-seek-ways-of-boosting-affordable-housing/a-79438939?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In many major urban centers of Europe, the housing shortage has become an explosive social issue. DW looks into various models that have been put in place across the continent.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Are Germans giving up their beloved meat and sausages?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6296a2c8622d6fbbb1a2c49bf5bab69b34d0c1cb24180a59e981fa598f9f863</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-are-germans-giving-up-their-beloved-meat-and-sausages/live-79441034--d9fb5f1aa888.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-are-germans-giving-up-their-beloved-meat-and-sausages/live-79441034?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germans used to be all about sausages and meat. While those do remain popular, things seem to be slowly changing. There also are new insights into the economic side of East Germany's espionage DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>B