ished>2026-09-22T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/princess-diana-s-brother-makes-explosive-claims-about-royals-in-new-memoir/a-79309465--3d900d102240.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/princess-diana-s-brother-makes-explosive-claims-about-royals-in-new-memoir/a-79309465?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Here are some of the key revelations from Charles Earl Spencer's highly anticipated memoir "Swan Song: Diana, My Sister." It has already provoked Buckingham Palace to react.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Trial starts of ex-Transport Minister Scheuer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06321eddd004263cdb2bc3b5ab3ab03cbabf786380ebec8e877cdf03df1d3c86</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-trial-starts-of-ex-transport-minister-scheuer/live-79351160--5052118e7b45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-trial-starts-of-ex-transport-minister-scheuer/live-79351160?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Transport Minister Andreas Scheuer is being tried for perjury related to a failed car toll scheme. And cherry farmers have brought in a bumper harvest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's car crisis: Can the 35-hour workweek survive?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d38c45a96542605fac2ee0cd8b7e8f381ef45c49d07c8ef98c6621ff24ff8ad2</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488--cb2e3220b33e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German carmakers want employees to work 40 hours instead of the current 35 without extra pay, arguing it would improve competitiveness. Unions strongly oppose the proposal and view it as an attack on workers' rights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>German state elections deal a blow to Chancellor Friedrich Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75713001aa21a3825f6c42e644aeb193cb2c9a292d54f70b363503024e910f77</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T21:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585--45dd8fc79779.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elections in Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania have dealt the CDU a historic defeat while the AfD saw a massive gain. The pressure on Germany's unpopular chancellor is mounting.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>AfD makes gains in state elections but has no government options</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:276d45c0853b7cca331a786b7470a8e73c4433eb480c0bba063e612b4b09c244</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T19:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-makes-gains-in-state-elections-but-has-no-government-options/a-79348308--1a6e760f93a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-makes-gains-in-state-elections-but-has-no-government-options/a-79348308?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite making significant gains in both Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, the far-right AfD remains without options to form a state government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces energy tax losses as EV sales rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9755d39710fc28bf53e48f48d6e8b707f1d8c1b337d052ef9cd95046356342d7</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422--82b05ee44dbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The rapid shift to electric vehicles in Germany is cutting fuel tax revenue for the government. As EV sales surge, policymakers face growing pressure to find new ways to fund roads and transportation infrastructure.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>In cosmopolitan Berlin, elections still closed to foreigners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dccb9f9734f264d88d10a936efa5cfe4d374a58234188bc434affaceb5c4bb44</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579--2c7a3b66c58f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter of Berlin residents will have no say in the German capital's city-state election because they lack citizenship. That's the highest proportion of residents excluded from the election yet, and many are unhappy.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Doctors offer Oktoberfest flu jabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09bc007032f013c2b8b0d73482aa39e64b27eedb4c8fdcd3b47c13ba0439cfef</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548--b4ec07a0d158.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https: