2b6bbc4079877a81e021f23a20a76d52bd2457cbcefbed</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410--afcfe0d2ce3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bloody May, student sit-ins and the squatter movement: Berlin has long been a hotbed for working-class organizing and radical left-wing politics.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football in Germany booming, but still much to do</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5ea10f43316743f98511babd761d8e3d4895445a968d33513bb342b953aa6ac</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T04:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687--313365dcb46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women's football is growing rapidly, particularly in Germany. Nevertheless, equal pay and investment remain major talking points.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz attacks spill oil into Persian Gulf</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19d6140c91c3e224d977291a5cd5b7d18cce82acae8149d025a3015b3c06cead</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092--09836173253c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As war disrupts one of the world's busiest shipping lanes, satellite images reveal that oil is spreading toward protected coral reefs and mangrove forests.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Dual citizenship means Germany now in competition for talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0537129a1a04fb2bfbc4497964f14a0827b2bf0ad86f39b773c4aed178eff4b5</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797--d43696518a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Coach Jürgen Klopp has named several players to his first Germany squad who are eligible to play for other countries. Some still aren't committed to playing for thje national team long-term.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Beethoven and Andy Warhol: Rebel icons on show in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d0e11fd1940a0da2ce3a14a8920938fb6a4e4ac4696d383360bc2eee764e6e7</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944--59ad6d6535a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new exhibition "Beethoven by Warhol" at the Beethoven House in Bonn presents the pop artist's late masterpiece: a picture of Ludwig van Beethoven. The exhibition shares the story of the work with the public.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>VAR's mission creep a problem for football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78e0298b1f33e7ad2dbb604d79367a5bb28c2e082cde2b3da1e3bf3808b648f8</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642--644b469bed29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a decade of use, questions around VAR in football are louder than ever. Has the technology strayed too far from its remit?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Ovechkin backs Putin party in campaign video</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab4c46c5606767961d04084a8c3a48ae92f8a588705857c417c40b18a55547aa</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772--a8049deceb76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey legend Alexander Ovechkin has lent Vladimir Putin's party a helping hand in its parliamentary election campaign. That's in keeping with a pattern of support by an athlete who claims not to be political.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Germany's football team to 'reclaim the flag'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a46516d9fbeb9031e0a8c3e39c60d30dcc7992f9b06f8f4f4b429246dce711f</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-germany-s-football-team-to-reclaim-the-flag/a-79307610--57ff88db5991.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-germany-s-football-team-to-reclaim-the-flag/a-79307610?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp, Germany's new head coach, says he wants his team to reclaim pride in being German after recent political developments.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Jews once lived lived here: When houses tell stories</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d00d9d0a57da268e33acf0af1ebc1c1e88e01f7dc7231ca362b0adfcbaf2450d</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jews-once-lived-lived-here-when-houses-tell-stories/a-79264813--f29d1ad1c32d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jews-once-lived-lived-here-when-houses-tell-stories/a-79264813?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Time and again, residents tracing the history of their homes discover the lives of Jewish predecessors who fled or were deported amid stories of suffering and loss.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp's first Germany squad includes 44 players</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a25fe35a34404d37e7b2b9ba8d4cc67a9e01bfd6c99c58347d2f08a050cf78f</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-s-first-germany-squad-includes-44-players/a-79289254--9874c23792d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-s-first-germany-squad-includes-44-players/a-79289254?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's new head coach Jürgen Klopp has named a huge squad for his first four games, splitting them into two groups. A host of new faces is included.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Saint, sinner or feminist icon: How Mary Magdalene's image evolved through time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64bc2f4620bf48c3d9f939af720b041b751f5ba73731e6d50e2d2cd3e374f0ef</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868--1a6f3ade345e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From "Apostle of the Apostles" to prostitute, Mary Magdalene has been assigned a wide variety of roles, as a new exhibition shows.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change worsened Nepal's deadly mountain collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d2d8dfa92bb49a1d6dd0c2617587934c640d1bca9718c67e75c1b3e4d84e8fd</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578--691d9083ccec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A glacier and rock collapse in Nepal killed nearly 1,400 people and left thousands missing. Scientists say decades of warming helped set the disaster in motion.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>After Neuer: Who will be Germany's new No. 1 goalkeeper?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c76d0c9ba7d5a25d214559b8dcc70e8a0294eca95171e50736f017cc3cec4d93</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377--1d35484fc587.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following Manuel Neuer's retirement, there are many candidates to succeed him, but which goalkeeper will Jürgen Klopp choose? What factors will play a role? And will Neuer's future have an indirect influence?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Global Gender Gap Report: Women's hard-won gains 'fragile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13ad7ce0d12fc9a8d48e73ba641911b1c71b25914830df0b832e893b03aad2b7</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086--9ed95bd98a77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two decades of progress toward gender parity is at risk as women's political representation declines, according to a new World Economic Forum report. At the current pace, the remaining gap could take 120 years to close.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>German drama 'Blindspot Berlin' revisits 2016 Christmas market attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6831b5623e4804d424fd45349a3831ff1fa2ff12c27663b6c24b07924229e920</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162--11e3e3b69ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the terrorist attack on a Berlin Christmas market, a new German miniseries looks into the institutional failures that allowed the deadly truck rampage to happen.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How extreme heat is hitting wallets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c99b8888747505710a463cc423f37fa0a7cfa16019cc04236fee0fa4c36aeef2</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-hotter-weather-is-making-us-poorer/a-79268306--10853d8a0a0a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-extreme-heat-is-hitting-wallets/a-79268306?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Heat waves, wildfires and floods have cascading economic impacts, causing incomes to decline and the price of basic goods to rise. The trend will escalate as temperatures continue to increase.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish scientists find first evidence of Diplodocus dinosaur in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86db5eefaaa473614ecd5e7c95091233acfb03c5ea8281a3b2b6a4bdf49535c9</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-scientists-find-first-evidence-of-diplodocus-dinosaur-in-europe/a-79277825--f2d2e7bb0613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-scientists-find-first-evidence-of-diplodocus-dinosaur-in-europe/a-79277825?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paleontologists in Spain say they have found the first evidence of the long-necked Diplodocus genus of dinosaur outside of North America. They found bones at the rich La Tejeria fossil site in Teruel in eastern Spain.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why the era of cheap government debt is over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0de2aced0f2f29db69f0d97432fb05bd23c91d2d6d9d8b3b937abae13ae17f47</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272--435550125c87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US debt has topped $40 trillion. How risky is the country's growing debt burden. And will investors keep funding Washington's deficits?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why AI researchers warn humanity could face extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e064b7d1d5fc1879b5b346a8a762e8a22fab5b5fa9035768374e6c8fb0bd941</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-ai-researchers-warn-humanity-could-face-extinction/a-79263146--d42b075a07d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-ai-researchers-warn-humanity-could-face-extinction/a-79263146?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Could artificial intelligence pose an existential threat to humanity? Some leading researchers are warning against an unregulated race toward AI superintelligence.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Iran and US: Two countries and the pistachio between them</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b03e988187b9762ccd1470000f27750d4e61877a460767da31c1132df1578878</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-and-us-two-countries-and-the-pistachio-between-them/a-79224310--28756f33fc8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-and-us-two-countries-and-the-pistachio-between-them/a-79224310?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pistachios sold across the United States have a surprising history: California's trees trace their roots to Iran. Now, both regions face the same threat — their farmland is sinking as groundwater disappears.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Women's Basketball World Cup: Can Germany harness a boom?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa9082828a05c0842da47e04d8be6ecbe545e5411c82ec0667974c99baf62d7f</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602--77d972e02866.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany thrilled fans at the Women's Basketball World Cup. But even if this sparked a boom in the women's game, the infrastructure simply isn't ready for it.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's richest man Dangote's IPO out of reach in Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cad65b8da9136d5333f1d4238a5c94ba45067de97129c5eb0cf8f5a29dac42ad</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398--03e0d1756308.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dangote seeks $1.6 billion from investors to finance a $14.3 billion expansion and thus double the oil refinery's capacity. The offer could give millions of Nigerians a stake in the company. But who can truly afford it?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The Crusades: How a medieval holy war still shapes politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07e5a92400e25efe8f4dc55b0b2a6b8ffb5e80c459e6ffd091872b40ac6f94d5</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-crusades-how-a-medieval-holy-war-still-shapes-politics/a-79203784--8fa07b173177.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-crusades-how-a-medieval-holy-war-still-shapes-politics/a-79203784?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 1095, the Catholic Church launched the Crusades: wars that left millions dead and whose legacy still shapes political and ideological conflicts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Can Iran replace sea trade with land routes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:035a14e43b672d9e1126a2957672c4d85353dbb0286b31d5f6d23ba02b5a49f9</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179--9748aa6cdc36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran is shifting trade toward northern ports and land routes as its southern shipping faces a US blockade. Analysts say the corridors can keep essential goods moving, but cannot replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Zverev wins US Open in golden year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff6b7cf0c46b72d48ced9079f3afd7284d12b86b66fd6d3882215f527f77f188</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T22:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706--d962ccd6a0c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev has won the US Open for the first time, defeating Ben Shelton in the final. It is Zverev's second Grand Slam win of 2026 after a long wait for his first title, but controversy still hangs over him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why are European banks moving gold out of United States?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38bee224cf6eaeaa8535e3ced72bfe7098fce4a101e6cf57e940d9fc5ffb27fa</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013--320ff1551fa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Netherlands and France have moved their gold out of US vaults. Part of the reason is fears about the reliability of the US, but equally important is the need to keep gold closer to home in the event of a crisis.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Corals as climate archive: Are El Nino events intensifying?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c430979a780de293d13934157af26311f2c5cc2b5b2c606de6de494dbd479569</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-nino-events-intensifying/a-79243425--ac4752671640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-nino-events-intensifying/a-79243425?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Records show that El Nino events have been frequent and often extreme over the past few decades. Is this normal? Or is it the result of climate change? Corals can give us a clear indication.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>India looks to steer BRICS away from anti-Western turn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e580c44fde12d615b40bcc18d822138371b8e7404bdf02cecb0d2fb6791afa4</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234--e9a076e9f28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit 2026 takes place in Delhi this weekend. Unlike last year, Putin and Xi are expected to attend. Can India keep the expanded bloc united?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>The 'end of an era' as Goethe-Institut in Russia closes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cda291875f6c2a46ade2bbe8b4c383d86d6ade670f648ba50137a0876ce33fe</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321--189393464061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Goethe-Institut was one of the last German institutions still operating in Russia. However, following Moscow's decision to close its offices, all employees will have to stop working by September 13.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Celine Dion became a pop culture icon across generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:964cb4c7cca8253a4b57e0d0ab74c882687519bc92f7f41dc6e4de399599a308</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-celine-dion-became-a-pop-culture-icon-across-generations/a-79213779--40db204d1ea8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-celine-dion-became-a-pop-culture-icon-across-generations/a-79213779?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the global star kicks off her anticipated Paris residency, here's how Celine Dion managed to gain younger followers while keeping her loyal older fans.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Belarusians still find hope in a silenced country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe0