t-for-the-sport/a-79199569?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Six months after Saudi Arabia pulled funding from the breakaway organization, LIV Golf have filed for bankruptcy protection. Several of the world's best players signed on to LIV, so where does that leave golf?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Conspiracy theories can provide answers but not peace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d98b7cd3a979365d93dd5d583c4791bcb2c2835588d11975bbe3b63590ceb8a</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/conspiracy-theories-can-provide-answers-but-not-peace/a-79022756--b464ce7f771c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/conspiracy-theories-can-provide-answers-but-not-peace/a-79022756?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Twenty-five years after 9/11, conspiracy theories about the terrorist attacks persist. But even as an attempt to make sense of a tragedy, psychologists say the benefit in conspiracy ideation or belief is short-lived.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>The billion-euro trade driving Europe's eels to extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e93dc7ef565d6fcb4de6a729308b5872c2ef5f86cf218ca6b73264a001c6d725</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145--e574ad564b10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Traffickers are making big bucks smuggling millions of critically endangered eels across continents, using suitcases on planes and legal loopholes to deliver them to dinnerplates. Where are the smuggling hotspots?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>The Bayeux Tapestry in London: What's behind the hype?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d63e626ed513c625b72d5719a1aea43dbda95e79204dac323c0a00adc3457310</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-bayeux-tapestry-in-london-what-s-behind-the-hype/a-78488629--9a9477f8929c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-bayeux-tapestry-in-london-what-s-behind-the-hype/a-78488629?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The exhibition of the Bayeux Tapestry at the British Museum is eagerly anticipated across the UK, as the medieval masterpiece is considered by many to be a symbol of the country's identity.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>PISA 2025 results: Reading and math scores plummet worldwide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2115b38c11b2cb2d41230860b6d5291a7a09188b5d9adb5b076353c404822bb</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pisa-test-reveals-alarming-drop-in-reading-and-math-skills/a-79147293--6fcb0a53f051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pisa-2025-results-reading-and-math-scores-plummet-worldwide/a-79147293?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The PISA 2025 results reveal record-low student performance, with digital distractions and AI use raising concerns. Germany is faring worse than ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f267f960be171ff835f0650454dda850757ff0c5d1bd7a81befc6ea3edd40583</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Croatia: Toxic waste protest draws tens of thousands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d890657ac3e2c2d734114d2c493b6d08506c748e2b3b8bace2c0bbdb68a6c9af</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T17:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228--9dec1bdce80c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Zagreb demonstrators demanded that the government come up with a plan to clear illegal toxic waste in 20 days. Prime Minister Plenkovic has promised to tackle the issue.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37de42eb13ff2f9ef2c68ba41b09026b6b10842cd38821edaf29830b6ffcc07c</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden environmental cost of AI data centers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fef6864c1f0a05a5dd72da998d06b902feb61765169271ccf7eb4684c09d97a7</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-environmental-cost-of-ai-data-centers/a-78789889--5e00024ffa87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-environmental-cost-of-ai-data-centers/a-78789889?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As data centers multiply to meet AI demand, they're straining power grids, draining water supplies and reshaping the land and air around them.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is Saxony-Anhalt's economy really struggling?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:872c8b5d00b2883870a4f9e7dcc4c26e02b62b9b132fcaffb805a36066841918</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143--acfa7a18352e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD party has long claimed that the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt has been left behind. Is that really the case? A closer look at the data offers some interesting insights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1de6fb61cd63bbb001a1a813f88a36100ca9afee5ed7d77fc598ac45fc183651</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Volkswagen's huge workforce became a costly burden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73f7d61a4b4b55d28b564087441cf8a198e7e0fbaf8cc09ee7282098f4bedd82</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-volkswagen-s-huge-workforce-became-a-costly-burden/a-77766154--6b1e762393dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-volkswagen-s-huge-workforce-became-a-costly-burden/a-77766154?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The struggling German carmaker plans to cut up to 100,000 jobs from its 630,000-strong workforce. How did VW's headcount get so bloated, and will the cuts be enough to survive the Chinese EV onslaught?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Is Germany's economic slump finally over?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:060e39ed183dae8384b7793e16f732fe0f84dc25e3c5d43bae56ecbdab26238c</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447--a101d614d4d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite a slew of negative headlines, the German economy has posted its best figures in years. There are reasons for optimism, but structural issues remain.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry></feed>
